# Gate step 2262-iyyu — an edit to the host-escape shim, or a cargo-nextest pin bump, in
# with-tillandsias-builder.sh reaches a host whose toolbox is already initialised.
# Both used to be skipped there: shims were installed only by the first init, and
# any executable cargo-nextest counted as the pinned one. The fixture runs the real
# functions with stub toolbox and curl and a scratch HOME.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking builder shims and nextest follow their pins on an initialised host (2262-iyyu)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-builder-installs-follow-their-pins.lua"
STEP_ERROR="an edited host-escape shim or a nextest pin bump would not reach an initialised host, or an unverified or foreign nextest was touched (2262-iyyu) — see the FAIL lines above"
STEP_OK="Builder shims and nextest follow their pins"
STEP_READS="scripts/lua/test-builder-installs-follow-their-pins.lua scripts/with-tillandsias-builder.sh"
